# Templates and Examples

Use these templates as a practical baseline.

## Template selection flow

```mermaid
flowchart TB
	A[Identify user need] --> B{Content type}
	B -->|Product capability and onboarding| C[Use Product template]
	B -->|Policy or standard decision| D[Use Guideline template]
	B -->|Operational response| E[Use Runbook template]
	B -->|Integration contract| F[Use API template]
```

## Product documentation template

```markdown
---
title: Product Name
description: What the product does and who it is for
last_reviewed_on: 2026-07-03
owner: product-team-name
---

# Product Name

## Overview
## Access and onboarding
## Core workflows
## Troubleshooting
## Support
```

Recommended additions:

1. Links to related APIs and runbooks.
2. Environment-specific access requirements.
3. Support channel and escalation route.

## Guidelines template

```markdown
---
title: Guideline Title
description: Decision guidance for a specific topic
last_reviewed_on: 2026-07-03
owner: team-name
---

# Guideline Title

## When to use
## Required standards
## Recommended approach
## Exceptions
## References
```

Recommended additions:

1. Clear mandatory versus optional guidance.
2. Date/version of policy review.
3. Exceptions with approval path.

## Runbook template

```markdown
---
title: Runbook Title
description: Operational response for a known scenario
last_reviewed_on: 2026-07-03
owner: on-call-team
---

# Runbook Title

## Trigger/alert condition
## Immediate checks
## Step-by-step actions
## Verification
## Rollback or recovery
## Escalation
```

Recommended additions:

1. Expected recovery time guidance.
2. Verification commands and success criteria.
3. Incident note template.

## API documentation template

```markdown
---
title: API Name
description: API capabilities and integration guidance
last_reviewed_on: 2026-07-03
owner: api-team
---

# API Name

## Base URL and environments
## Authentication
## Endpoints
## Request/response examples
## Errors and retry guidance
## Rate limits
```

Recommended additions:

1. Versioning and deprecation policy.
2. Authentication token lifecycle notes.
3. Error examples with remediation guidance.

## Example repository setup

1. Start from [template-documentation-site](https://github.com/ministryofjustice/template-documentation-site).
2. Configure workflows, ownership, and metadata conventions.
3. Add content folders for product docs, guidelines, runbooks, and APIs.
4. Validate locally before PR.

## End-to-end template usage example

1. Start with Product template to publish user-facing overview.
2. Add API template for integration details.
3. Add Runbook template for support/ops workflows.
4. Add Guideline template for policy and standards.
5. Cross-link all four pages for discoverability.
